# RULE: TypeScript, React, Electron, Zustand

Applies to TypeScript/React code. Architecture boundaries: `.cursor/rules/00-core.mdc`.

## TypeScript

Never: `any`, `@ts-ignore`, `as unknown as`, untyped IPC/WebSocket/event payloads, **any `@deprecated` API** in TS/React/Electron/Node/DOM/deps.

Before using a library symbol: check `@deprecated` JSDoc; use replacement; no suppress without ADR.

Prefer: discriminated unions, branded IDs, explicit public return types, `unknown` at boundaries + narrowing, immutable event payloads.

Forbidden examples: React `FormEvent`/`FormEventHandler`; DOM prefer `SubmitEvent`/`ChangeEvent`/`InputEvent`.

## React / Hooks / Zustand

Components: render, props, hooks, forward intent — no SIP/Electron/repos/business rules/legacy operator platform parsing.

Hooks: selectors, Use Case binding, local UI — no telephony rules, SIP sessions, infra calls.

Zustand: projections only — no Use Cases/adapters/repos/SIP/Electron/business rules.

## Electron

**Main:** lifecycle, windows, tray, updates, notifications, files, OS — no call rules, React/Domain state, legacy operator platform rules.

**Preload:** minimal typed APIs, narrow allowlists, validate payloads — no raw `ipcRenderer`, no Node globals in renderer.

**IPC:** typed channels with request/response/error shape, owning context, security — no ad hoc channel names in components.

## External inputs

Validate at boundaries (narrow from `unknown`): IPC, WebSocket, SIP metadata, host-page, config, storage. Domain receives trusted typed values.

Browser APIs → UI/adapters/infra. Node APIs → infra. Domain imports neither.

## Completion check

- No `any` or `@deprecated` in touched code
- `npm run lint` passes (`@typescript-eslint/no-deprecated`)
- No infra import in Domain; no SIP in UI/store
- IPC typed and validated
